    },
    "lifecycle_state" : "DRAFTED",
    "details" : {
      "en" : {
        "id" : "en",
        "purpose" : "To calculate the total sum for the Glasgow Modified Alcohol Withdrawal Scale (GMAWS) to assess and monitor the severity of alcohol withdrawal symptoms (AWS) in hospitalized adult patients.",
        "keywords" : [
          "glasgow",
          "modified",
          "alcohol ",
          "withdrawal",
          "scale",
          "GMAWS",
          "tremor",
          "sweating",
          "hallucinations",
          "orientation",
          "agitation"
        ],
        "use" : "Use to assess and monitor alcohol withdrawal symptoms in adult inpatients undergoing supervised withdrawal management. \n\n- The score is calculated by adding the points of the individual variables:\n- Tremor: None 0 points, Present with arms extended 1 point, Present with arms at rest 2 points\n- Sweating: None 0 points, Moist skin 1 point, Drenching sweat 2 points\n- Hallucinations: None 0 points, Uncertain, or patient reports but not distressed 1 point, Present and distressed 2 points\n- Orientation: Orientated 0 points, Uncertain or disoriented in one domain 1 point, Disoriented in ≥2  domains 2 points\n- Agitation: None 0 points, Anxious/restless 1 point, Distressed or pacing 2 points\n\nThe total sum guides symptom-triggered therapy (e.g., benzodiazepine dosing) and timing of reassessment.\n\nThe GMAWS provides an objective and structured alternative to CIWA-Ar, reducing inter-rater variability and improving adherence to withdrawal protocols.\nValidated primarily in inpatient and medical detox settings.",
        "misuse" : "Not to be used for assessing patients who are acutely intoxicated, for outpatient alcohol withdrawal management, or as a substitute for clinical judgment in unstable or complex withdrawal cases.",
        "copyright" : "© Cambio CDS"
      }
    },
    "other_details" : {
      "references" : "McPherson A, Benson G, Forrest EH. Appraisal of the Glasgow assessment and management of alcohol guideline: a comprehensive alcohol management protocol for use in general hospitals. QJM. 2012 Jul;105(7):649-56. doi: 10.1093/qjmed/hcs020. Epub 2012 Feb 10. PMID: 22328545.\n\nSchonewald B, Hunter K, Ely AV, Heil J, Ganetsky V, Milburn C, Rafeq R, Salzman M. Impact of an alcohol withdrawal screening and treatment protocol for hospitalized patients. J Subst Use Addict Treat. 2024 Sep;164:209443. doi: 10.1016/j.josat.2024.209443. Epub 2024 Jun 12. PMID: 38871256.",
      "en" : "An assessment scale used to evaluate and monitor the severity of alcohol withdrawal symptoms (AWS) in hospitalized adult patients."
    }
  },
